POW.SYSTEMS =E2=80=94 Source + Transformation Dossier Core rule

*Data-garden moat =3D unique transformation =C3=97 continuous collection =
=C3=97 time*

POW should not collect data because it is interesting. Every source should
feed a common event pipeline:

OBSERVE =E2=86=92 ARCHIVE RAW =E2=86=92 NORMALIZE =E2=86=92 RESOLVE IDENTIT=
Y =E2=86=92 DIFF =E2=86=92 EMIT EVENT =E2=86=92
TRANSFORM =E2=86=92 JOIN =E2=86=92 ACTION =E2=86=92 OUTCOME

Universal object:

*physical resource =C3=97 capability =C3=97 constraint =C3=97 person =C3=97=
 place =C3=97 time*

The source is never the moat by itself. The moat is the historical
transformed state and the joins/outcomes built over it.
1. GRID / ELECTRICITY NESO Transmission Entry Capacity / connection
registers

Source:
https://www.neso.energy/data-portal/transmission-entry-capacity-tec-registe=
r/tec_register

Collect:

   - project ID/name
   - developer/owner
   - capacity MW
   - technology
   - connection point
   - connection date
   - gate/status
   - row additions/removals/changes

Cadence:

   - each official release; currently Tuesday/Friday for TEC register
   - archive raw every release forever

Transformations:

   - entered_queue
   - capacity_changed
   - connection_date_moved
   - gate_changed
   - owner_changed
   - disappeared
   - connected
   - probable_cancelled

Derived:

   - queue_age
   - date_slippage_days
   - project_survival_rate
   - MW_added / MW_removed
   - MW_at_risk
   - developer delivery rate
   - queue churn
   - speculative_queue_score
   - connection_probability by region/technology/developer
   - constraint_pressure by node

Join:
NESO =C3=97 DNO headroom =C3=97 planning =C3=97 Companies House =C3=97 REPD=
 =C3=97 grid
reinforcement =C3=97 site/property
UK Power Networks / live network state

Open-data portal:
https://open-data.org.uk/

Important dataset family:
UKPN National Energy Outage / network operational feeds

Collect:

   - live faults/outages
   - affected geography
   - start/end time
   - restoration updates
   - network constraint events
   - curtailment
   - power flow/headroom where available
   - flexibility events

Transformations:

   - outage_started
   - outage_updated
   - outage_restored
   - constraint_started
   - constraint_relaxed
   - curtailment_event
   - reinforcement_effect

Derived:

   - outage frequency
   - outage duration survival curve
   - restoration reliability
   - local reliability score
   - constraint-hours
   - curtailment-hours
   - grid stress index
   - local power scarcity
   - reliability trend

Join:
site/UPRN =C3=97 EV =C3=97 solar =C3=97 battery =C3=97 compute =C3=97 busin=
ess =C3=97 grid node
Northern Powergrid headroom / capacity

API/data portal:
https://northernpowergrid.opendatasoft.com/explore/dataset/heatmapdemanddat=
a/api/

Collect:

   - firm capacity
   - max demand
   - contracted demand
   - generation
   - constraints
   - fault levels
   - demand headroom
   - generation headroom
   - planned interventions

Transformations:

   - headroom_delta
   - constraint_intensification
   - constraint_relaxation
   - planned_capacity_added
   - contracted_capacity_consumed

Derived:

   - spare_capacity_ratio
   - headroom_velocity
   - connection_pressure
   - node_constraint_score
   - expected_relaxation_time

Elexon

Developer portal:
https://developer.data.elexon.co.uk/

Collect:

   - system prices
   - demand
   - generation
   - imbalance
   - BM data
   - constraint-related market state
   - standing/reference data where useful

Transformations:

   - electricity_input_cost
   - volatility
   - scarcity periods
   - generation mix state
   - system stress

Derived:

   - productive electricity cost
   - mining/inference electricity threshold
   - battery opportunity windows
   - price volatility
   - price =C3=97 grid-constraint joins

Important:
Raw Elexon history is already strong, so use mainly as JOIN/TRANSFORMATION
substrate rather than pretending archive alone is a moat.
Octopus / household tariff APIs

Use:

   - import tariff
   - export tariff
   - agile/time-of-use price
   - tariff region
   - standing charge
   - pricing window

Transformations:

   - actual energy input cost by 30m/time period
   - best charge/discharge window
   - compute marginal cost
   - EV charge cost
   - solar/battery arbitrage state

Derived:

   - =C2=A3/kWh productive cost
   - charge_now / delay / export decision
   - effective annual tariff profile

2. EV / MOBILITY Public Charge Point Regulations / OCPI

Guidance:
https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/the-public-charge-point-regulati=
ons-2023-guidance/public-charge-point-regulations-2023-guidance

Key fact:
Public CPOs must expose machine-readable reference + availability data and
status changes quickly; historical availability is not required to be
preserved.

This is a core time-moat feed.

Collect per EVSE:

   - operator
   - immutable location/location ID
   - EVSE ID
   - connector
   - power
   - tariff
   - AVAILABLE
   - CHARGING
   - RESERVED
   - OUTOFORDER
   - INOPERATIVE
   - timestamp

Cadence:

   - consume feed/webhook/OCPI status at appropriate near-real-time cadence
   - preserve every state transition

Transformations:

   - availability transition tape
   - outage episode
   - occupancy episode
   - tariff change
   - connector state change

Derived:

   - true uptime
   - mean time between failures
   - mean time to recovery
   - occupancy pressure
   - unavailable-hours
   - site saturation
   - operator reliability
   - connector reliability
   - effective price/kWh history
   - geographic charger scarcity
   - local EV charging pressure

